R if detected\n236. ❌ The system supports custom agents by implementing Agent interface\n237. ✅ Agents receive AgentInput containing session, runId, messages, tools, state, systemPrompt\n238. ✅ Agents receive EventEmitter to emit AG-UI protocol events\n239. ✅ Agents return AgentResult indicating success, optional error, and updated conversation history\n\n### AG-UI Protocol Implementation\n\n240. ✅ The system emits RUN_STARTED event with threadId, runId, input, and timestamp\n241. ✅ The system emits MESSAGES_SNAPSHOT event with current messages\n242. ✅ The system emits STATE_SNAPSHOT event with current application state\n243. ✅ The system emits TEXT_MESSAGE_START event with messageId and role='assistant'\n244. ✅ The system emits TEXT_MESSAGE_CONTENT event with messageId and delta text\n245. ✅ The system emits TEXT_MESSAGE_END event with messageId\n246. ✅ The system emits TOOL_CALL_START event with toolCallId and toolCallName\n247. ✅ The system emits TOOL_CALL_ARGS event with toolCallId and delta JSON arguments\n248. ✅ The system emits TOOL_CALL_END event with toolCallId\n249. ✅ The system emits RUN_FINISHED event with threadId, runId, and final result text\n250. ✅ The system emits RUN_ERROR event with error message when runs fail\n251. ✅ The system routes all events to connected clients via Socket.IO 'event' message\n\n### Tool Definition and Execution\n\n252. ✅ The system accepts tool definitions with name, description, JSON Schema, and confirmationRequired flag\n253. ✅ The system merges client-side tools with MCP-provided tools before forwarding to agents\n254. ✅ For client-side tools, system stores promise-based resolver in session.pendingToolCalls\n255. ✅ The system receives tool results via tool_result messages\n256. ✅ The system resolves pending tool call promise with tool result content\n257. ✅ For JSON Schema tool parameters, system converts ToolDefinition to AI SDK tool format\n258. ✅ The system creates execute functions for each tool (client or MCP remote 